        "modelAnswerEn": "1. Common Error: Using scalar addition for vector components.\n2. Correct Fact: Always resolve vectors into rectangular components (Rx = ΣAx, Ry = ΣAy) before finding resultant.\n3. Scientific Reason: Vectors add geometrically, not algebraically.\n4. Board Recommendation: Examiners specifically penalize this confusion; ensure you state the proper causal mechanism.",
