        "modelAnswerEn": "1. Definition: Primary biological mechanism in Chapter 6: Behaviour.\n2. Governing Mechanism: Innate behaviours (kinesis, taxis, simple reflexes, fixed action patterns, instincts) contrasted with learned behaviours (habituation, imprinting, classical and operant conditioning)....\n3. Mathematical / Structural Model: Requires labeled diagrams with correct scientific terminology.\n4. Practical Application: Widely utilized in experimental setups and modern scientific technology across Pakistan.",
