      {
        "id": "ex_class_12_biology_6_conc2",
        "questionNumber": "Conceptual Q2",
        "category": "short_question",
        "titleEn": "Critical Distinction in Behaviour",
        "titleUr": "باب 6: رویہ میں عام امتحانی غلطی اور درست تصور",
        "marks": 4,
        "questionEn": "What common conceptual error do students make regarding Behaviour? State the correct scientific fact with reasoning.",
        "questionUr": "باب 6: رویہ میں کون سی غلط فہمی پائی جاتی ہے؟ سائنسی دلیل کے ساتھ درست جواب دیں۔",
        "modelAnswerEn": "1. Common Error: Confusing kinesis with taxis.\n2. Correct Fact: Kinesis is non-directional movement where speed changes with intensity; taxis is directional orientation toward or away from a stimulus.\n3. Scientific Reason: Directionality is the defining scientific distinction.\n4. Board Recommendation: Examiners specifically penalize this confusion; ensure you state the proper causal mechanism.",
        "modelAnswerUr": "1. عام غلطی: Confusing kinesis with taxis.\n2. درست تصور: Kinesis is non-directional movement where speed changes with intensity; taxis is directional orientation toward or away from a stimulus.\n3. سائنسی دلیل: Directionality is the defining scientific distinction.",
        "boardTipEn": "Examiners design trick questions around this specific mistake.",
        "boardTipUr": "یہ بورڈ امتحانات کا پسندیدہ ٹرکی سوال ہے۔"
      }
